{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a Cp*Co(III)-catalyzed synthesis of multi-substituted isoquinolines via site-selective C-H activation of unsymmetrical O-acyloximes. The cobalt catalyst demonstrates superior site selectivity at the sterically less hindered position compared to Cp*Rh(III) catalysts, particularly when using terminal alkynes. The reaction is redox-neutral, utilizing the N-O bond of the oxime as an internal oxidant.",
